<p>Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said President Donald Trump is applying “undue pressure” on Ukraine as Washington pushes for a negotiated end to the nearly four-year war with Russia, arguing that demands should not fall disproportionately on Kyiv. In interviews cited by multiple outlets, Zelensky said it is “not fair” if the spotlight is mainly on Ukraine’s concessions while Russia faces less pressure at the table. Zelensky also warned that any peace plan that requires Ukraine to give up territory—especially areas Russia has not captured—would be unacceptable to Ukrainians, and he suggested such a proposal would fail if put to a referendum. Even with the blunt pushback, his comments point to active diplomacy, with Kyiv signaling it wants a settlement that can hold over time—not one that would be seen at home as a forced loss.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/SpRFZJy1nNpQaj5Ugda2iAz_76Pe8oFsTHsMiI6hyds7THjRLneXr0534LK63CAsNvc7UT5ws7eNWL6SKpWBVel-9rGcyr8LCieZwau5WoAWgxo_mWQ49I_591BHt4BFIWhcKfNM_MBHQaS_zDF9IxIu5PlCdvacTm0HybTmoHm5cCt-Z2QzoXs' alt='President Donald Trump and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky pictured amid renewed peace talks coverage.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Negotiation posture: Zelensky said he is “not such a person” to fold easily under pressure and, per RT, told US interlocutors Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner not to push Ukraine into what Ukrainians would see as an “unsuccessful story”.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelensky (Ukraine): He said it was “not fair” for US peace demands to focus mainly on Ukraine’s concessions and argued that any plan requiring Ukraine to give up territory Russia has not captured would be rejected by Ukrainians if put to a referendum. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3343864/zelensky-says-trumps-peace-demands-focused-only-ukraine-not-fair'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Volodymyr Zelensky (Ukraine): He urged US negotiators not to “give victory” to Russia and said he hoped pressure was a tactic rather than a decision; RT also reported he rejected Moscow’s demand that Kyiv drop its claims to Russia’s four new regions and Crimea and withdraw troops from parts of the Donbass under its control. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/632692-zelensky-pleas-us-envoys-victory/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Kremlin (Russia): Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov has said Putin is open to a one-on-one meeting with Zelensky, but only at the final stage of negotiations, according to RT. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/632692-zelensky-pleas-us-envoys-victory/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3343864/zelensky-says-trumps-peace-demands-focused-only-ukraine-not-fair'>Zelensky says Trump’s peace demands focused only on Ukraine ‘not fair’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/ukraines-zelenskiy-says-trump-exerting-undue-pressure-on-him'>Ukraine’s Zelensky says Trump exerting undue pressure on him</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/ukraine-president-volodymyr-zelensky-says-trump-exerting-undue-pressure-on-him-over-peace-deal-11051430#publisher=newsstand'>Zelensky Says Trump Exerting Undue Pressure On Him Over Peace Deal</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/not-fair-zelenskyy-says-trump-is-pressuring-ukraine-more-than-russia-amid-talks-to-end-war-13981022.html'>‘Not fair’: Zelenskyy says Trump is pressuring Ukraine more than Russia amid talks to end war</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/632692-zelensky-pleas-us-envoys-victory/'>Zelensky urges US negotiators not to ‘give victory’ to Russia</a> - rt.com</li></ul>